module
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter11.ChosenNaturalSource.LocalGeometry.Preliminary.Residual.Multiplicity.ActorKernel
public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter12.Section02.ReductionSource.SeedAlternativesNormalizerBound
public import CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterD.Section02.FittingOffenders.SourcePrime
public import Theory.GroupTheory.PGroup.OmegaCoprimeAction
public import Theory.GroupTheory.GeneralizedFitting.MovedComponent

/-!
# Actual cubic actors and their component kernels on the full natural orbit

The original qrc theorem supplies a minimal cubic actor on the faithful
N_G(L)-image of V_M. Reducedness kills the two-core of precisely this image.
The original full SL₃ marking makes its component normal and quasisimple.

Every nonzero component-invariant subspace has binary dimension at least
3n: project its natural-copy coordinates onto a nonzero coordinate and use
irreducibility. Thus D.2.13's four-dimensional five-core support cannot occur.
Every minimal cubic actor centralizes the odd prime cores other than the
three-core. In even degree, a two-subgroup centralizing the component also
centralizes the entire three-core, including higher powers: the ambient rank
bound makes that core cyclic and its first omega lies in the component.

Consequently the actual component kernel of a minimal cubic actor centralizes
Fitting. If nontrivial, it moves an actual component J, whose A-orbit is
contained in the original component centralizer and generated by commutators
with that same kernel. The earlier rank exclusion makes J prime to three.
The final theorem selects the actor and gives this alternative on D,S without
extra input premises. It does not exclude the remaining three-free component
or bound multiplicity in the faithful alternative. Those obligations remain
with qt-d-1222-natural-preliminary-source, and qt-d-1222-natural-local-geometry
retains final chapter assembly.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, D.2.13, pp.184--185; the nonfaithful argument of
D.3.9, pp.200--201; 3.2.5, p.580; and 11.0.4, p.760, combined manuscript
of 1 March 2004.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory Representation Representation.BinaryOffender
open scoped MatrixGroups IsMulCommutative
open CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter12.Section02
open CFSG.Quasithin.ChapterB.QuasisimpleSource
